---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
const company = import.meta.env.COMPANY_NAME || 'AI Page Audit';
const contact = import.meta.env.SUPPORT_EMAIL || 'support@citerank.app';
---
<Site title="Terms of Service — AI Page Audit" description="The terms governing use of AI Page Audit's AEO analysis tools.">
  <section class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p>Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <main>
    <article class="legal wrap">
      <div class="note">These terms are provided in good faith and in plain language. They are not a substitute for legal advice — have a qualified lawyer review them before you rely on them commercially.</div>

      <h2>1. What AI Page Audit does</h2>
      <p>AI Page Audit fetches web pages using the identifying headers of AI and search crawlers, analyses the HTML those crawlers receive, and reports on how readable and citable that content appears to be. It is a diagnostic and advisory tool.</p>

      <h2>2. No guarantee of results</h2>
      <p><strong>We do not and cannot guarantee that following AI Page Audit's recommendations will cause any AI engine or search engine to cite, rank, index or mention your content.</strong> Those systems are operated by third parties, change without notice, and make their own decisions. Anyone promising guaranteed AI visibility is misrepresenting how these systems work. AI Page Audit reports what crawlers can read and where gaps exist; what an engine then does with your content is outside our control.</p>

      <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
      <p>You need an account to run checks. You are responsible for keeping your password secure and for activity under your account. One account is intended for one person — sessions are single-active by design, so signing in on a new device ends the previous session. Sharing credentials across a team is not supported and may result in suspension.</p>

      <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may check pages you own, operate, or have a legitimate professional reason to analyse (for example, competitor research or client work). You may not use AI Page Audit to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Send high-volume automated requests to third-party sites, or use it as a proxy for scraping.</li>
        <li>Attempt to bypass usage metering, credit limits, or authentication.</li>
        <li>Resell raw AI Page Audit output as an automated service without a written agreement with us.</li>
        <li>Check content that is unlawful in your jurisdiction or ours.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We fetch third-party pages on your instruction. You are responsible for having the right to request analysis of a given URL.</p>

      <h2>5. Checks, credits and plans</h2>
      <p>Each account receives one free check. Beyond that, access is either a one-time credit pack or a monthly Pro subscription. A check is consumed when a live URL fetch is attempted. <strong>If we cannot retrieve the page at all, the check is automatically returned to your balance.</strong> Analysing HTML you paste yourself does not consume a check.</p>
      <p>Purchased credits do not expire. Pro subscriptions are activated manually after payment verification and run for 30 days from activation.</p>

      <h2>6. Payment</h2>
      <p>Payments are currently made by UPI transfer and activated manually once we verify the transaction reference against our records. We do not collect, process or store card details. Activation typically happens within one business day. See our <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>7. Availability</h2>
      <p>We aim for continuous availability but do not promise uninterrupted service. Analysis depends on third-party sites being reachable and on AI provider APIs; either may fail independently of us. Scheduled maintenance and provider outages happen.</p>

      <h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, {company}'s total liability arising from your use of the service is limited to the amount you paid us in the three months preceding the claim. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, including lost traffic, lost rankings, lost revenue or lost business opportunity.</p>

      <h2>9. Suspension and termination</h2>
      <p>We may suspend or close an account that breaches these terms, abuses the metering system, or submits fraudulent payment claims. You may stop using the service at any time. Unused credits in an account closed by us for cause are forfeited; unused credits in an account you close voluntarily are handled under the <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the "last updated" date above, and continued use after a change constitutes acceptance.</p>

      <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India, and the courts of India have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.</p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <style>
    .legal { max-width: 760px; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 32px 0 10px; }
    .legal p, .legal li { font-size: 15.5px; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.72; }
    .legal ul { padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
    .legal strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .note { background: var(--accent-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.6; }
  </style>
</Site>
